Electrical safety is based on the Electrical Safety Act and the National Electrical Safety Board's regulations **ELSÄK-FS**. The goal is to prevent *personal injury* and fires caused by electricity.

## Key concepts

- Power current and voltage ranges
- Authorisation and self-inspection
- Working without voltage as the ground rule
- Safety procedures and working methods

## Work on or near electrical installations

1. Disconnect the installation from voltage
2. Secure against reconnection
3. Verify absence of voltage
4. Earth and short-circuit when needed

### Authorisation

> Only those with the required knowledge who have been assigned the work may perform electrical work.

| Regulation | Area |
| ---------- | ---- |
| ELSÄK-FS | Electrical safety generally |
| SS-EN 50110 | Operation of electrical installations |

```sh
search "ELSÄK-FS" --scope el
```

